# A refusal in the port's own words, carrying no marker: the php
# PortGroup's Xcode 12 guard (portgroups/php-1.1.tcl) sets known_fail
# and refuses in pre-fetch. Dockhand's pre-flight records known_fail
# ports unsupported before any VM boots, so this log is what a guest
# writes when a refusal reaches it anyway — and the conservative
# reading keeps it failed, with the port's own complaint as the detail
# (the ui_error line precedes the phase line, so it is the first
# substantive Error) and the environment kept. The phase line names
# the port itself, so nothing is blamed.
# RECONSTRUCTED from the PortGroup's guard, not captured: see README.md.
port: php56-apcu
outcome: failed
state: failed
detail: php56-apcu @4.0.11 cannot currently be compiled with Xcode 12 or later
lint: clean
